{"step_index":9,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-24T02:18:38Z","content":"Created At: 2026-08-24T07:48:38+05:30\nCompleted At: 2026-08-24T07:48:38+05:30\nFile Path: `file:///C:/Users/renu5/.gemini/config/skills/prompt-forge/references/patterns.md`\nTotal Lines: 83\nTotal Bytes: 6165\nShowing lines 1 to 83\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n1: # Credit-Killing Patterns Reference\r\n2: \r\n3: 37 patterns that waste tokens and cause re-prompts. Read this file when the user pastes a bad prompt and asks you to fix it, or when diagnosing why a prompt is underperforming.\r\n4: \r\n5: ---\r\n6: \r\n7: ## Task Patterns\r\n8: \r\n9: | # | Pattern | Bad Example | Fixed |\r\n10: |---|---------|------------|-------|\r\n11: | 1 | **Vague task verb** | \"help me with my code\" | \"Refactor `getUserData()` to use async/await and handle null returns\" |\r\n12: | 2 | **Two tasks in one prompt** | \"explain AND rewrite this function\" | Split into two prompts: explain first, rewrite second |\r\n13: | 3 | **No success criteria** | \"make it better\" | \"Done when the function passes existing unit tests and handles null input without throwing\" |\r\n14: | 4 | **Over-permissive agent** | \"do whatever it takes\" | Explicit allowed actions list + explicit forbidden actions list |\r\n15: | 5 | **Emotional task description** | \"it's totally broken, fix everything\" | \"Throws uncaught TypeError on line 43 when `user` is null\" |\r\n16: | 6 | **Build-the-whole-thing** | \"build my entire app\" | Break into Prompt 1 (scaffold), Prompt 2 (core feature), Prompt 3 (polish) |\r\n17: | 7 | **Implicit reference** | \"now add the other thing we discussed\" | Always restate the full task — never reference \"the thing we discussed\" |\r\n18: \r\n19: ---\r\n20: \r\n21: ## Context Patterns\r\n22: \r\n23: | # | Pattern | Bad Example | Fixed |\r\n24: |---|---------|------------|-------|\r\n25: | 8 | **Assumed prior knowledge** | \"continue where we left off\" | Include Memory Block with all prior decisions |\r\n26: | 9 | **No project context** | \"write a cover letter\" | \"PM role at B2B fintech, 2yr SWE experience transitioning to product, shipped 3 features as tech lead\" |\r\n27: | 10 | **Forgotten stack** | New prompt contradicts prior tech choice | Always include Memory Block with established stack |\r\n28: | 11 | **Hallucination invite** | \"what do experts say about X?\" | \"Cite only sources you are certain of. If uncertain, say so explicitly rather than guessing.\" |\r\n29: | 12 | **Undefined audience** | \"write something for users\" | \"Non-technical B2B buyers, no coding knowledge, decision-maker level\" |\r\n30: | 13 | **No mention of prior failures** | (blank) | \"I already tried X and it didn't work because Y. Do not suggest X.\" |\r\n31: \r\n32: ---\r\n33: \r\n34: ## Format Patterns\r\n35: \r\n36: | # | Pattern | Bad Example | Fixed |\r\n37: |---|---------|------------|-------|\r\n38: | 14 | **Missing output format** | \"explain this concept\" | \"3 bullet points, each under 20 words, with a one-sentence summary at top\" |\r\n39: | 15 | **Implicit length** | \"write a summary\" | \"Write a summary in exactly 3 sentences\" |\r\n40: | 16 | **No role assignment** | (blank) | \"You are a senior backend engineer specializing in Node.js and PostgreSQL\" |\r\n41: | 17 | **Vague aesthetic adjectives** | \"make it look professional\" | \"Monochrome palette, 16px base font, 24px line height, no decorative elements\" |\r\n42: | 18 | **No negative prompts for image AI** | \"a portrait of a woman\" | Add: \"no watermark, no blur, no extra fingers, no distortion, no text overlay\" |\r\n43: | 19 | **Prose prompt for Midjourney** | Full descriptive sentence | \"subject, style, mood, lighting, composition, --ar 16:9 --v 6\" |\r\n44: \r\n45: ---\r\n46: \r\n47: ## Scope Patterns\r\n48: \r\n49: | # | Pattern | Bad Example | Fixed |\r\n50: |---|---------|------------|-------|\r\n51: | 20 | **No scope boundary** | \"fix my app\" | \"Fix only the login form validation in `src/auth.js`. Touch nothing else.\" |\r\n52: | 21 | **No stack constraints** | \"build a React component\" | \"React 18, TypeScript strict, no external libraries, Tailwind only\" |\r\n53: | 22 | **No stop condition for agents** | \"build the whole feature\" | Explicit stop conditions + ✅ checkpoint output after each step |\r\n54: | 23 | **No file path for IDE AI** | \"update the login function\" | \"Update `handleLogin()` in `src/pages/Login.tsx` only\" |\r\n55: | 24 | **Wrong template for tool** | GPT-style prose prompt used in Cursor | Adapt to File-Scope Template (Template G) |\r\n56: | 25 | **Pasting entire codebase** | Full repo context every prompt | Scope to only the relevant function and file |\r\n57: \r\n58: ---\r\n59: \r\n60: ## Reasoning Patterns\r\n61: \r\n62: | # | Pattern | Bad Example | Fixed |\r\n63: |---|---------|------------|-------|\r\n64: | 26 | **No CoT for logic task** | \"which approach is better?\" | \"Think through both approaches step by step before recommending\" |\r\n65: | 27 | **Adding CoT to reasoning models** | \"think step by step\" sent to o1/o3 | Remove it — reasoning models think internally, CoT instructions degrade output |\r\n66: | 28 | **Expecting inter-session memory** | \"you already know my project\" | Always re-provide the Memory Block in every new session |\r\n67: | 29 | **Contradicting prior work** | New prompt ignores earlier architecture | Include Memory Block with all established decisions |\r\n68: | 30 | **No grounding rule for factual tasks** | \"summarize what experts say about X\" | \"Use only information you are highly confident is accurate. Say [uncertain] if not.\" |\r\n69: \r\n70: ---\r\n71: \r\n72: ## Agentic Patterns\r\n73: \r\n74: | # | Pattern | Bad Example | Fixed |\r\n75: |---|---------|------------|-------|\r\n76: | 31 | **No starting state** | \"build me a REST API\" | \"Empty Node.js project, Express installed, `src/app.js` exists\" |\r\n77: | 32 | **No target state** | \"add authentication\" | \"`/src/middleware/auth.js` with JWT verify. `POST /login` and `POST /register` in `/src/routes/auth.js`\" |\r\n78: | 33 | **Silent agent** | No progress output | \"After each step output: ✅ [what was completed]\" |\r\n79: | 34 | **Unlocked filesystem** | No file restrictions | \"Only edit files inside `src/`. Do not touch `package.json`, `.env`, or any config file.\" |\r\n80: | 35 | **No human review trigger** | Agent decides everything autonomously | \"Stop and ask before: deleting any file, adding any dependency, or changing the database schema\" |\r\n81: | 36 | **Vague first turn on Opus 4.7 / 4.8** | \"fix the auth bug\" with no scope, no files, no criteria | Opus 4.7 and 4.8 read prompts literally — they no longer fill implicit context like 4.6 did. Use Template M. Front-load intent, file scope, constraints, and acceptance criteria. |\r\n82: | 37 | **Context rot on long sessions** | Keeps correcting in the same session for 60+ turns | New task = new session. Use /rewind instead of correcting. /compact at ~50% context. Subagents for file-heavy investigation. |\r\n83: \nThe above content shows the entire, complete file contents of the requested file.\n"}
