ion — 🟢 Lower priority\n- **7 areas where prompt-forge is already stronger** than Promptive Sentry (37 failure patterns, agentic prompt engineering, prompt injection defense, premise sanity checking, model-specific optimization, template library, anti-sycophancy vocabulary enforcement)\n- **Priority ranking table** of gaps\n- **\"What to give me\" section** listing 6 specific materials for deeper analysis, with emphasis on extracting the extension's source JS files from `C:\\Users\\renu5\\AppData\\Local\\Google\\Chrome\\User Data\\Default\\Extensions\\ikbkijdgnelcijmdkcaaoabmobagakim\\`\n\n### Research — COMPLETE\n- Chrome Web Store page returned raw HTML/CSS/JS, no readable content\n- Web search confirmed extension identity and features (3 searches performed)\n- Identified the IDE version (VS Code extension on Open VSX) with its 7-layer context engine\n\n## 4. Model Knowledge\n\n- **Chrome Web Store pages** render via JavaScript and return no useful content via `read_url_content`. The page for this extension returned only CSS/JS bundles — no description, no feature list. Web search was the only way to get extension details.\n- **Promptive Sentry has two versions:** (1) Chrome browser extension for ChatGPT/Claude/Gemini, (2) IDE extension (VS Code/Cursor/Windsurf/Antigravity) with the 7-layer context engine. The IDE version is more technically detailed.\n- **Prompt-forge skill structure:** Main SKILL.md (265 lines) with Primacy Zone (identity, hard rules, output format), Middle Zone (execution logic: mode detection, intent extraction, model routing, diagnostics), and Recency Zone (verification). Reference files: `templates.md` (453 lines, 13 templates A-M) and `patterns.md` (83 lines, 37 failure patterns).\n- **Anti-sycophancy skill** has 3 layers: Input Debiasing, Critical Response Strategy (11 rules), Sentence Pattern Enforcement (banned openers, banned vocabulary, structural tell detection, response structure). It includes cross-enforcement with prompt-forge (vocabulary scanning on generated prompts).\n\n## 5. Files and Code\n\n### Edited Files\n- **`C:\\Users\\renu5\\.gemini\\antigravity\\brain\\fa1b1897-231d-4b72-b32d-1b687a3ba964\\gap_analysis.md`** — CREATED. Full gap analysis artifact. ~200 lines covering all 8 gaps, 7 strengths, priority ranking, and materials request.\n\n### Viewed Files\n- **`C:\\Users\\renu5\\.gemini\\config\\skills\\prompt-forge\\SKILL.md`** (265 lines) — Full skill definition. Key sections: Mode Detection table (lines 54-59), Intent Extraction 9 dimensions (lines 63-75), Model Routing with Gemini vs Opus rules (lines 96-130), Antigravity Platform Patterns (lines 133-170), Diagnostic Checklist (lines 175-205), Template Auto-Selection table (lines 212-225).\n- **`C:\\Users\\renu5\\.gemini\\config\\skills\\prompt-forge\\references\\templates.md`** (453 lines) — 13 templates (A-M). Notable: Templates A-F are standard frameworks, G is File-Scope for IDEs, H is ReAct + Stop Conditions, I-K are visual/image, L is Prompt Decompiler, M is Opus 4.7/4.8 Task Brief.\n- **`C:\\Users\\renu5\\.gemini\\config\\skills\\prompt-forge\\references\\patterns.md`** (83 lines) — 37 credit-killing patterns organized by category: Task (1-7), Context (8-13), Format (14-19), Scope (20-25), Reasoning (26-30), Agentic (31-37).\n- **`C:\\Users\\renu5\\.gemini\\config\\skills\\anti-sycophancy\\SKILL.md`** (342 lines) — Full anti-sycophancy defense system. Identity signal \"Priyanshu,\" prefix (line 25), 3 layers, 11 rules, banned vocabulary list (lines 222-276), pre-delivery self-audit (lines 332-341).\n- **Chrome Web Store page content** saved to `.system_generated/steps/5/content.md` — raw HTML/CSS/JS, not useful for analysis.\n\n## 6. Current Work and Next Steps\n\n### What was just completed\nThe gap analysis artifact was delivered. The user has not yet responded to it.\n\n### What the user likely wants next\n1. **Provide extension source files** — The user may extract the Chrome extension's JS source from their local Chrome installation and share it for deeper reverse-engineering analysis\n2. **Implement specific gaps** — The user may pick gaps from the priority list and ask to modify the prompt-forge SKILL.md, templates.md, or patterns.md files\n3. **Ask follow-up questions** about specific gaps or the priority ranking\n\n### Customization files read (must re-read)\n- **`C:\\Users\\renu5\\.gemini\\config\\skills\\prompt-forge\\SKILL.md`** — The skill being analyzed and potentially modified. Core to the entire task.\n- **`C:\\Users\\renu5\\.gemini\\config\\skills\\anti-sycophancy\\SKILL.md`** — Activated by user for honest feedback. Must re-read to maintain the \"Priyanshu,\" prefix, banned vocabulary, pre-delivery self-audit, and counter-argument requirements.\n- **`C:\\Users\\renu5\\.gemini\\config\\skills\\prompt-forge\\references\\templates.md`** — Template library that may need new templates added.\n- **`C:\\Users\\renu5\\.gemini\\config\\skills\\prompt-forge\\references\\patterns.md`** — Failure patterns reference that may need expansion.\n\nYou have the 1 following artifacts written to the artifacts directory:\n\n[ARTIFACT: gap_analysis]\nPath: file:///C:/Users/renu5/.gemini/antigravity/brain/fa1b1897-231d-4b72-b32d-1b687a3ba964/gap_analysis.md\nLast Edited: 2026-08-24T02:20:53Z\n\n# Conversation Logs\n\nReference the following log files for the full, untruncated conversation:\n\n- C:\\Users\\renu5\\.gemini\\antigravity\\brain\\fa1b1897-231d-4b72-b32d-1b687a3ba964\\.system_generated\\logs\\transcript.jsonl\n\n**IMPORTANT: this summary is just for your reference. You may respond to my previous and future messages, but DO NOT ACKNOWLEDGE THIS CHECKPOINT MESSAGE. JUST READ IT BUT DO NOT MENTION IT, RESPOND TO IT, OR TAKE ACTION BECAUSE OF IT.**"}
